==English==

===Pronunciation===
* (''UK''): {{enPR|krō'kā}}, {{IPA|/ˈkrəʊkeɪ/}} or {{IPA|/ˈkrəʊkɪ/}}, {{SAMPA|/"kr@UkeI/}}
* (''US''): {{enPR|krōkā'}}, {{IPA|/kroʊˈkeɪ/}}, {{SAMPA|/kroU"keI/}}

===Noun===
{{wikipedia}}
{{en-noun|s|-}}

# {{uncountable}} A [[game]] played on a [[lawn]], in which players use [[mallet]]s to drive [[wooden]] [[ball]]s through [[hoop]]s ([[wicket]]s)
# {{countable}} A [[shot]] in this game in which the [[opponent]]'s ball is driven away by hitting one's own ball when they are in contact
# {{countable}} A [[croquette]].

====Derived terms====
* [[croquet set]]


===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# {{transitive}} To drive (the one's opponent's ball) by striking one's own ball placed against it.
# {{intransitive}} To croquet one's opponent's ball.

